{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35733850",
      "title": "Navigating between Pages with Links",
      "sourceHash": "0aa29b9ec7d17dd28ccaef0412a456874e5093ebf1e88bc3968f374ad79907be",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.55,
          "end": 5.19,
          "en": "Now that we saw this alternative approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.19,
          "end": 8.46,
          "en": "let's dive back into more routing features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.46,
          "end": 12.33,
          "en": "that apply to both types of route definitions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.33,
          "end": 15.9,
          "en": "And if we take a look at our basic example app here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.9,
          "end": 19.83,
          "en": "at the moment, we of course, might notice one big flaw.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.83,
          "end": 23.79,
          "en": "At the moment, we always have to manually edit the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.79,
          "end": 26.01,
          "en": "if we wanna navigate from the starting page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.01,
          "end": 28.74,
          "en": "to the products page and vice versa.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.74,
          "end": 31.11,
          "en": "And it's, of course, not very realistic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.11,
          "end": 34.47,
          "en": "that we want our users to use this website like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.47,
          "end": 36.21,
          "en": "because how would users know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.21,
          "end": 39.303,
          "en": "which kind of paths are supported here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.32,
          "end": 42.24,
          "en": "Of course, we typically wanna provide links",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.24,
          "end": 43.35,
          "en": "on the page instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.35,
          "end": 45.27,
          "en": "And we can, of course, do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.27,
          "end": 47.85,
          "en": "We could, for example, go to the HomePage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.85,
          "end": 52.54,
          "en": "and there we could add some text below the title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.52,
          "end": 54.93,
          "en": "with a paragraph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.93,
          "end": 57.36,
          "en": "And for example, say Go to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.36,
          "end": 60.66,
          "en": "and then add a link with the default anchor element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.66,
          "end": 64.83,
          "en": "and say the list of products.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.83,
          "end": 66.39,
          "en": "Something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.39,
          "end": 71.16,
          "en": "And this default HTML anchor element takes a ref attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.16,
          "end": 74.52,
          "en": "which could lead to /products.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.52,
          "end": 76.71000000000001,
          "en": "That's how we could add a link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.71000000000001,
          "end": 80.82,
          "en": "If we do that, we'll see that the link appears here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.82,
          "end": 83.85,
          "en": "And if we click it, we go to The Products Page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.85,
          "end": 85.8,
          "en": "So that's working, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.8,
          "end": 87.45,
          "en": "Well, kind of.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.45,
          "end": 90.63,
          "en": "We have a problem with this approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.63,
          "end": 93.6,
          "en": "If you watch this refresh icon here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.6,
          "end": 97.8,
          "en": "as I click on the link, you will see that it briefly flashes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.8,
          "end": 101.67,
          "en": "and turns to a cross and back to a refresh icon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.67,
          "end": 102.503,
          "en": "The reason for that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 102.503,
          "end": 105.93,
          "en": "is that technically, we're sending a new request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.93,
          "end": 109.22999999999999,
          "en": "to the server that's serving this website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.22999999999999,
          "end": 113.55,
          "en": "Now, that server will serve back that single HTML page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.55,
          "end": 116.28,
          "en": "that makes up this single page application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.28,
          "end": 117.53999999999999,
          "en": "but what happens under the hood",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.53999999999999,
          "end": 121.05,
          "en": "is that we, of course, load all the JavaScript code again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.05,
          "end": 123.78,
          "en": "load the entire React application again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.78,
          "end": 127.17,
          "en": "and restart the React application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.17,
          "end": 130.38,
          "en": "That's a lot of unnecessary work under the hood",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.38,
          "end": 133.83,
          "en": "that can also impact the site performance,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 133.83,
          "end": 135.72,
          "en": "which we typically wanna avoid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.72,
          "end": 138.48,
          "en": "because we already loaded all the JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 138.48,
          "end": 139.82999999999998,
          "en": "We don't wanna load it again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.82999999999998,
          "end": 143.4,
          "en": "and we don't wanna restart the React application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 143.4,
          "end": 145.47,
          "en": "We would also lose any context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 145.47,
          "end": 149.04,
          "en": "or application-wide state if we do so.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 149.04,
          "end": 151.02,
          "en": "So we don't wanna switch the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 151.02,
          "end": 154.59,
          "en": "by sending a new HTTP request to the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.59,
          "end": 156.81,
          "en": "With that, we lose all the benefits",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 156.81,
          "end": 159.213,
          "en": "of single page applications after all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 160.07999999999998,
          "end": 162.32999999999998,
          "en": "Instead, we wanna have a link like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 162.32999999999998,
          "end": 166.02,
          "en": "but under the hood, it should just change the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 166.02,
          "end": 169.56,
          "en": "and set it to the URL we're trying to navigate to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 169.56,
          "end": 173.67000000000002,
          "en": "but it should then prevent the default of sending a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 173.67000000000002,
          "end": 177.99,
          "en": "and instead let React Router know about the new URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 177.99,
          "end": 181.53,
          "en": "and ensure that React Router loads the appropriate element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 181.53,
          "end": 183.9,
          "en": "for that new URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 183.9,
          "end": 187.68,
          "en": "And that can be implemented with another special component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.68,
          "end": 191.34,
          "en": "that can be imported from react-router-dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 191.34,
          "end": 194.16,
          "en": "And here I'm importing it in this Home.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 194.16,
          "end": 196.653,
          "en": "because that's where I wanna add this link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 197.49,
          "end": 199.71,
          "en": "The new component we wanna import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 199.71,
          "end": 203.55,
          "en": "from react-router-dom is called Link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 203.55,
          "end": 204.78,
          "en": "And as the name suggests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 204.78,
          "end": 206.823,
          "en": "we can use it to construct a link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 207.72,
          "end": 211.82999999999998,
          "en": "We use it instead of the default anchor element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 211.82999999999998,
          "end": 213.75,
          "en": "And it doesn't have a ref attribute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 213.75,
          "end": 216.45,
          "en": "Instead, we use the to attribute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 216.45,
          "end": 219.84300000000002,
          "en": "But there we then still specify the path we wanna go to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 221.01,
          "end": 223.23,
          "en": "Now, what the link component does under the hood",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 223.23,
          "end": 226.41,
          "en": "is it does render an anchor element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 226.41,
          "end": 230.37,
          "en": "but it basically listens for clicks on that element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 230.37,
          "end": 232.14,
          "en": "prevents the browser default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 232.14,
          "end": 236.07,
          "en": "of sending a HTTP request if the link is clicked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 236.07,
          "end": 237.87,
          "en": "and instead simply takes a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 237.87,
          "end": 241.11,
          "en": "at the route definitions to update the page accordingly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 241.11,
          "end": 243.63,
          "en": "and load the appropriate content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 243.63,
          "end": 245.73,
          "en": "It will also change the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 245.73,
          "end": 248.583,
          "en": "but without sending a new HTTP request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 249.69,
          "end": 252.18,
          "en": "So if we create this link here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 252.18,
          "end": 254.7,
          "en": "we still see the link here on this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 254.7,
          "end": 257.97,
          "en": "but if I now click it, and you watch this refresh icon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 257.97,
          "end": 259.65,
          "en": "you see that it doesn't flash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 259.65,
          "end": 262.92,
          "en": "and we don't send a new HTTP request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 262.92,
          "end": 266.58,
          "en": "Instead, here, we can now use this link,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 266.58,
          "end": 269.31,
          "en": "which is provided by react-router-dom",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 269.31,
          "end": 272.25,
          "en": "and that is how we should navigate between pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 272.25,
          "end": 273.963,
          "en": "with react-router-dom.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}